    "perplexity": {
      "description": "Graffiti Soul is the fifteenth studio album of original material by Simple Minds, released in 2009 on Sanctuary and later associated with Universal in some listings. It marked a strong late-career return for the Scottish band, pairing their characteristic arena-sized rock with polished pop-rock hooks and a more contemporary sheen. The album reached No. 10 in the UK and was issued in multiple formats, including a deluxe edition.\n\nRecorded after a long gap between albums, Graffiti Soul features the singles “Rockets,” “Stars Will Lead the Way,” and “This Is It,” along with title track standouts such as “Moscow Underground” and “Light Travels.” Critics and fans often viewed it as a revitalized, more confident statement that revisited the group’s melodic, atmospheric strengths while keeping the arrangements direct and accessible.",
